  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Under the Giza Plateau in Egypt, home of the great pyramids, radar scans are said to show 'something like a network of underground tunnels.' Filippo Biondi, a scientist who scanned beneath the pyramids in 2025 together with a colleague named Armando Mei, tells Michels this from his own work. He says the tomographic data, images built up in slices from the scans, showed 'a mess' of reflections, which if right would mean large hidden structures below the plateau."
}
